    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316-a1">

                <pb facs="0554" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1878/pg492"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    796.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terashima to Mr
                            Bingham.</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-05-14"><hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 14,
                        1878</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to hereby inform you that
                    this morning, at 8 a.m., Okubo Toshimichi, councilor of state and minister of
                    the interior, while on his way to call on the Emperor, was attacked and wounded
                    by assassins, at Kirvaricho Kojimachi, and has since died.</p>
                <p>With respect and consideration,</p>
                <closer><signed>TERASHIMA MUNENORI</signed>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">His
                        Imperial Japanese Majesty’s Minister for Foreign Affairs</hi>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency <hi rendition="#small-caps">John A. Bingham</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of
                            the United States in Japan</hi>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
